---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="About · Hotlines" description="How the World Emergency & Hotlines directory works: data sourcing, verification, routing, and privacy.">
  <article class="prose prose-invert mx-auto max-w-2xl text-fg">
    <h1 class="font-display text-4xl text-fg">About this project</h1>
    <p class="text-fg-muted">
      World Emergency & Hotlines is an open directory of every crisis, emergency, and support line we can
      verify, for every country on Earth. We think nobody should have to search in a panic.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-display mt-8 text-2xl text-fg">If you're in crisis right now</h2>
    <div class="rounded-2xl border border-danger/40 bg-danger/10 p-4 not-prose mb-6">
      <p class="text-sm text-fg-muted">
        Call your country's emergency number. In most of Europe: <span class="font-mono text-fg">112</span>.
        US/Canada: <span class="font-mono text-fg">911</span>. UK: <span class="font-mono text-fg">999</span>.
        Australia: <span class="font-mono text-fg">000</span>. These numbers work even without a SIM card on most networks.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-fg-muted">
        For crisis support: <a href="/category/suicide_crisis" class="text-accent hover:underline">find a crisis line →</a>
      </p>
    </div>

    <h2 class="font-display mt-8 text-2xl text-fg">How to use this site</h2>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-6 text-fg-muted">
      <li>
        <strong class="text-fg">Search</strong> by country, category, or service name (e.g. "Italy domestic violence",
        "UK childline", "Canada veterans").
        Use the filter chips to narrow to verified-only, SMS-accessible, or online-chat services.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong class="text-fg">Browse by category</strong> — see <a href="/categories" class="text-accent hover:underline">all 29 categories</a>
        with counts and verification coverage.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong class="text-fg">Explore the map</strong> — click any country to see all local numbers and crisis lines.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong class="text-fg">Country pages</strong> show hotlines grouped by category, with a "best available help"
        panel at the top and a traveller note about international dialling.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="font-display mt-8 text-2xl text-fg">How verification works</h2>
    <p class="text-fg-muted">
      Every hotline record carries a verification status. We never hide a record — we label its confidence level
      so you can make an informed decision.
    </p>
    <dl class="space-y-3 not-prose mt-4">
      {[
        ['verified_web',       'bg-success/15 text-success border-success/40',  'Confirmed against the organisation\'s own official website. Highest confidence.'],
        ['verified_authority', 'bg-success/15 text-success border-success/40',  'Confirmed directly with an authoritative source such as a government body.'],
        ['verified_knowledge', 'bg-success/10 text-success border-success/30',  'Confirmed against a trusted reference. High confidence.'],
        ['cross_referenced',   'bg-accent/15 text-accent border-accent/40',     'Found in multiple independent sources. Reliable but not yet checked against the official site. Treat as trustworthy; worth a quick verify for critical use.'],
        ['legacy_unverified',  'bg-fg-muted/15 text-fg-muted border-fg-muted/30', 'From an earlier dataset. Has not been independently confirmed. Please check the organisation\'s official website before relying on this number.'],
        ['disputed',           'bg-danger/15 text-danger border-danger/40',     'Conflicting information found. Treat with caution — the number may be wrong.'],
        ['deprecated',         'bg-fg-muted/15 text-fg-muted border-fg-muted/30', 'Believed to be no longer active. Included for reference.'],
      ].map(([status, tone, desc]) => (
        <div class="flex gap-3 items-start">
          <span class={`chip shrink-0 border text-[11px] mt-0.5 ${tone}`}>{(status as string).replace(/_/g, ' ')}</span>
          <p class="text-sm text-fg-muted">{desc}</p>
        </div>
      ))}
    </dl>

    <h2 class="font-display mt-8 text-2xl text-fg">Best-available routing</h2>
    <p class="text-fg-muted">
      On each country page, the site automatically selects the "best available help" — a verified crisis line if one
      exists, falling back to verified mental health support, then to unverified lines if that's all we have. This is
      surfaced prominently so that someone in distress doesn't need to scan a long list.
    </p>
    <p class="text-fg-muted mt-2">
      The same logic applies to the search: when you type a country + category, verified lines rank higher. Filter chips
      let you explicitly restrict results to verified or channel-specific services.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-display mt-8 text-2xl text-fg">Travellers & expats</h2>
    <p class="text-fg-muted">
      Most freephone/toll-free numbers require a local SIM or network connection for the country. If you're abroad:
    </p>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-6 text-fg-muted">
      <li><span class="font-mono text-fg">112</span> reaches emergency services in most countries even without a SIM.</li>
      <li>Look for hotlines with online chat (💬) — these work internationally over Wi-Fi.</li>
      <li>SMS-based lines (📱) may also work internationally depending on your roaming plan.</li>
      <li>Hotel staff and local emergency numbers will always have up-to-date local contacts.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="font-display mt-8 text-2xl text-fg">Privacy</h2>
    <p class="text-fg-muted">
      The search runs entirely in your browser — your search terms and results never leave your device.
      No queries are logged. The emergency banner reads your browser language setting only (no server call, no location).
      We don't use tracking cookies or analytics that identify individuals.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-display mt-8 text-2xl text-fg">Open data & contributing</h2>
    <p class="text-fg-muted">
      The entire dataset is open. Download it from the <a href="/data" class="text-accent hover:underline">data page</a>
      in JSON format. To contribute corrections or new hotlines, open a pull request or issue on GitHub.
    </p>
    <div class="not-prose mt-4 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
      <a href="/data" class="btn-primary">Data downloads →</a>
      <a href="https://github.com/craigrallen/world-emergency-hotlines/issues" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn-ghost">Report an error ↗</a>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
